hadiths[289]{hadithnumber,text}:
"752","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi that when Adam (peace be upon him) performed Hajj, the angels met him and said: O Adam (peace be upon him), your Hajj has been accepted. We performed Hajj two thousand years before you."
"753","Abu Salih Al-Hanafi narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Hajj is (like) jihad and ‘umrah is a voluntary act of worship."""
"754","Muhammad bin ‘Abbad bin Ja‘far narrates that we were sitting with ‘Abdullah bin ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) when I heard him say: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: Who is the one who has performed Hajj (i.e., what are the signs of one performing Hajj)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The one with disheveled hair and who keeps away from perfume.” Another man stood up and asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the means (sabeel)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Provision for the journey and a riding animal.”"
"755","It is narrated from the companion of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that he reports: I asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) about a man who has not performed Hajj, so should he take a loan to perform Hajj? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""No."""
"756","Ibn Jurayj says: I said to Nafi‘ (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Have you heard ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) mention the names of the months of Hajj?"" Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""Yes, he used to mention Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa‘dah, and Dhu al-Hijjah."" Ibn Jurayj says: I said to Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him), ""What if a man pronounces the Talbiyah for Hajj and enters Ihram before these months?"" Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) replied: ""I have not heard anything from him regarding this."""
"757","It is narrated from Abu al-Zubair that he heard from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked about a man who assumes the Ihram for Hajj before the months of Hajj. He replied: No."
"758","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) designated the places for entering into Ihram, he said: ""A man may benefit from his family (wife) and his clothes until he reaches that place which is for entering into Ihram."""
"759","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he stated: In Medina, a man from among the people of Medina stood in the mosque and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! From where do you command us to enter into Ihram?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The people of Medina should enter into Ihram from Dhu'l-Hulaifa, the people of Syria from Juhfa, and the people of Najd from Qarn (al-Manazil)."" Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him) says that Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) told me that he also understood that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""And the people of Yemen should enter into Ihram from Yalamlam."""
"760","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Madinah should assume ihram from Dhu'l-Hulaifah, the people of Shaam from Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn (al-Manazil)."" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: They (the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them) understood that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And the people of Yemen should assume ihram from Yalamlam."""
"761","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The people of Madinah were commanded to assume Ihram from Dhu’l-Hulayfah, the people of Syria from Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn (al-Manazil). Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: These are the three places which I myself heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I have been informed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “And the people of Yemen should assume Ihram from Yalamlam.”"
"762","Tawoos narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) fixed Dhu’l-Hulaifah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfah for the people of Syria, Qarn al-Manazil for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen. Then he said: “These are for the residents of those places and for those who come to them who are not residents there, and who intend to perform Hajj or Umrah; these are the places from where they should enter into ihram. But those whose residence is between the miqat and Makkah should enter into ihram from the place where they start their journey, until the people of Makkah should enter into ihram from Makkah itself.”"
"763","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that regarding the places for entering into Ihram, it is reported from the Prophet (peace be upon him) in the same manner as the hadith of Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) concerning the Miqats."
"764","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he stated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed Dhu’l-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfah for the people of Syria, Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and Qarn (al-Manazil) for the people of Najd. And those whose residence is between the miqat and Makkah, they should assume ihram from the place where they begin their journey."
"765","It is narrated from Abu Az-Zubair that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was asked about the place for entering into Ihram. He said: ""I heard it,"" then he fell silent. I think he was referring to the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""The people of Madinah will enter into Ihram from Dhu'l-Hulaifah, those coming from another route from Juhfah, the people of Iraq from Dhat 'Irq, the people of Najd from Qarn al-Manazil, and the people of Yemen from Yalamlam."""
"766","Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fixed Dhu’l-Hulaifa as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfa for the people of the West, Dhat ‘Irq for the people of the East, Qarn for the people of Najd, and for those among the people of Yemen or others who take the route of Najd, their miqat is Qarn al-Manazil, and for the people of Yemen, Yalamlam."
"767","Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him) says: I consulted ‘Ata’ (may Allah have mercy on him) and said: People think that the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not appoint Dhat ‘Irq as a miqat, and that at that time there were no people from the east. ‘Ata’ said: At that time there was no Iraq, but there were people from the east. ‘Ata’ said: We have heard in this way that the Prophet (peace be upon him) appointed Dhat ‘Irq or ‘Aqiq as the place for the people of the east to don ihram. And he said: At that time there was no Iraq, but there were people from the east. They did not attribute this statement to anyone among the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) other than the Prophet (peace be upon him), but they deny (that the Prophet did not appoint a miqat), rather they say that the Prophet (peace be upon him) appointed it as a miqat."
"768","It is narrated from Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not appoint Dhat 'Irq as a miqat, nor were there people from the east at that time. Rather, it is the people who have appointed Dhat 'Irq as a miqat. Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: In my opinion as well, the matter is as Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) has stated, and better knowledge is with Allah."
"769","Abu Al-Sha’tha’ says: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not appoint any miqat for the people of the east; it was the people who, based on Qarn, designated Dhat ‘Irq."
"770","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned the Hajj of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and he was instructed to recite the Talbiyah from there, and the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When you proceed towards Mina while walking, recite the Talbiyah."""
"771","It is narrated from Abu Sha’tha’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) returning anyone who passed the miqat without entering into ihram."
"772","It is narrated from Mihrash al-Ka‘bi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set out from Ja‘ranah at night and (entered Makkah and) performed ‘Umrah, and in the morning he was at Ja‘ranah, as if he had spent the night there."
"773","This hadith is narrated in the same way from another chain by Ibn Jurayj. Ibn Jurayj says that it is not ""Muharrash"" but ""Mukhrash."" Imam Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, says: Ibn Jurayj has spoken correctly because his son Mukhrash is with us."
"774","Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered me to seat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) behind me and take her, and to perform ‘Umrah for her from Taneem."
"775","It is narrated from Ibn al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) performed Umrah twice in a year: once from Dhul-Hulaifah and once from Juhfah."
"776","It is narrated from Qasim bin Muhammad (may Allah have mercy on him) that the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), performed Umrah twice in a year. Sadaqah bin Yasar says: I asked, ""Did anyone object to her?"" So Qasim (may Allah have mercy on him) (in astonishment) said: ""Subhan Allah!"" He said, ""Objection to the Mother of the Believers!"" Sadaqah says: I felt ashamed for having said this."
"777","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) performed two Umrahs every year during the era of Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"778","One of the sons of Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we were in Makkah with Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him). When the hair on his head would grow out, he would set out again to perform ‘Umrah."
"779","It is narrated from Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There is an ‘Umrah in every month."
"780","It is narrated from Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There is an ‘Umrah in every month."
"781","It is narrated from Qasim bin Muhammad (may Allah be pleased with him) that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) performed Umrah twice in one year, or he said, several times. Sadaqah says: I asked, did anyone object to her? Sadaqah says: Qasim said: (Object) to the Mother of the Believers! Sadaqah says: I felt ashamed."
"782","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) performed Umrah several times in one year, and said this here twice."
"783","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) assumed Ihram from Bayt al-Maqdis."
"784","Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered me to take Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) to perform Umrah, so I took her to perform Umrah from Taneem. She, or someone else besides her, said in the hadith: the night of Al-Muhassab."
"785","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform ghusl (ritual bath) on the days of Eid, on Fridays, on the day of Arafah, and when he intended to enter into the state of Ihram."
"786","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): She said that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would enter into the state of Ihram, I used to apply perfume to him for his Ihram, and likewise, before he became lawful after performing the Tawaf of Ziyarat of the House of Allah."
"787","Abdur Rahman bin Qasim narrates from his father, who narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and she spread both her hands and said: I applied perfume with these two hands of mine to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for Ihram when he assumed Ihram, and likewise for becoming lawful (halal) before performing the Tawaf of Ziyarat of the House of Allah."
"788","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: I applied perfume with my own hands to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for Ihram when he entered into Ihram, and likewise for becoming lawful (halal) after the circumambulation (Tawaf) of the House of Allah, before he became lawful."
"789","Urwah narrates that I heard Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) say: I applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for entering into Ihram and for coming out of Ihram. Urwah says: I asked Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), ""Which perfume?"" She replied: ""The best perfume."" Uthman says: Hisham did not narrate this hadith from anyone except me."
"790","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I saw the shine of fragrance in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) three days after (he had entered into) Ihram."
"791","Hasan bin Zaid narrates from his father, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) in the state of Ihram, and there was fragrance on his head like syrup."
"792","Aisha bint Saeed says: I applied musk and zareerah (types of fragrance) to my father at the time of Ihram."
"793","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Hajj Ifrad."
"794","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had assumed Ihram only for Hajj."
"795","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Hajj Ifrad."
"796","Aswad reports from Abdullah (that is, Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him) that he gave the ruling for Hajj Ifrad. He said: I said, they have preferred that each of the two should have a state of dishevelment and travel, and their opinion is that Hajj Qiran is superior. When someone asks them for a legal verdict, they give that verdict, whereas Abdullah himself disliked Hajj Qiran."
"797","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with the intention of performing Hajj, until when we reached the place of Sarif or near it, I began menstruating. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came and I was crying. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What has happened to you, have you started menstruating?"" I said, yes. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is something Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam, so complete all the rites of Hajj except for the Tawaf of the House (Ka'bah)."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered a sacrifice of a cow on behalf of his wives."
"798","Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that when Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, finished collecting the charities and came (to Mecca), the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, asked him: ""O Ali! For what have you entered into Ihram?"" He replied: ""For that which the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, has entered into Ihram."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Then offer a sacrifice, and remain in your state of Ihram."""
"799","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who describes the Hajj of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: ""We set out with the Prophet ﷺ, until when we were at the place of Baida, I looked ahead of me, to my right, to my left, and behind me, and I saw riders and pedestrians as far as the eye could see. Everyone wanted to complete this (Hajj), and everyone was striving to do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying. We had no intention except for Hajj, nor did we know anything else, nor did we know about ‘Umrah (during the months of Hajj). When we were at Marwah after the Tawaf, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'O people! Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should come out of Ihram, and let his Ihram for Hajj become an Ihram for ‘Umrah (i.e., the Tawaf and Sa’i have been done, and the acts of ‘Umrah are complete). If what I have come to know now had come to my knowledge earlier, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal.' So those who did not have a sacrificial animal came out of Ihram."""
"800","It is narrated from Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both), she states: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (for Hajj), so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal should come out of the state of Ihram."" And I did not have a sacrificial animal, so I came out of Ihram, and Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) had a sacrificial animal, so he did not come out of Ihram."
"801","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: There were still five days left in Dhu al-Qi'dah when we set out with the Prophet (peace be upon him) with the intention of Hajj. When we were at Sarif or near it, the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered that whoever did not have a sacrificial animal should turn his ihram (for Hajj) into an ihram for Umrah. And when we were in Mina, beef was brought to me. I asked, ""What kind of meat is this?"" It was said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has offered a sacrifice on behalf of his wives."" Yahya said: I narrated this hadith to Qasim bin Muhammad, and he said, ""Umrah! By Allah, you have brought the hadith in its original form."""
"802","From another chain, the same hadith is narrated from Umrah and Qasim, just like the chain of Sufyan (may Allah have mercy on him), without any difference in meaning."
"803","Tawoos says that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Madinah, but he ﷺ did not mention Hajj or Umrah; rather, he was waiting for revelation. When he ﷺ was between Safa and Marwah, revelation came down at that time. So he ﷺ ordered those companions who had put on the Ihram (for Hajj) and did not have a sacrificial animal with them to make it Umrah instead. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""If I had known earlier what I came to know later, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal. But I have stuck my hair (i.e., completed the rites) and brought the sacrificial animal, so now I cannot come out of Ihram without offering the sacrifice."" Suraqah bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up towards you ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Decide for us as if we are a people who have just been born. Is this Umrah only for this year or forever?"" You ﷺ said: ""Rather, it is forever. Now Umrah during the (days of) Hajj has been included until the Day of Resurrection."" Tawoos said: (In Makkah) Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived from Yemen, so the Prophet ﷺ asked him: ""With what intention did you put on Ihram?"" One of Maysarah or Hisham bin Hujairah narrated from Tawoos that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""With the Ihram of the Prophet ﷺ (i.e., with the same intention as you ﷺ did),"" and the other said: ""I am present with the Hajj of the Prophet ﷺ."""
"804","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both), he states that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed in Madinah for nine years and did not perform Hajj. Then (in the tenth year) he announced among the people for Hajj. People began to come to Madinah to set out with him (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out (for Hajj) and we also set out with him (ﷺ). We intended only Hajj and set out for that purpose alone. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was among us, and the Qur'an was being revealed to him (ﷺ), and he (ﷺ) knew its true meaning well, and he (ﷺ) acted as he was commanded. When we reached Makkah and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Tawaf of the House and the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, he (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal should make it an 'Umrah, and if what I have come to know later had been known to me earlier, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal and would have made it an 'Umrah."""
"805","Tawoos says that the Prophet ﷺ went out and he was not mentioning Hajj or Umrah by name, rather he was awaiting revelation. Tawoos said that when he ﷺ was making rounds between Safa and Marwah, revelation descended upon him. The Prophet ﷺ then ordered his companions, may Allah be pleased with them, that whoever among them had entered into Ihram for Hajj and did not have a sacrificial animal with him, should make it Umrah instead. Then he said: ""If I had known beforehand what I came to know later, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal, but I have already stuck to my intention and brought the sacrificial animal with me, so it is not permissible for me to become lawful (exit Ihram) without offering the sacrifice."" Then Suraqah bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up towards the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will you make a ruling about us as if we are a new people born today? Is this act of converting Hajj into Umrah specific to this year of ours, or is it permitted forever?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""It is permitted forever; Umrah has been included in the (days of) Hajj until the Day of Judgment."" He said that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, entered (Makkah) from Yemen, so the Prophet ﷺ asked: ""With what intention did you enter into Ihram?"" One of Ibn Tawoos or Ibrahim bin Maisarah said: ""I entered into Ihram and recited the Talbiyah like the Ihram of the Prophet ﷺ,"" and the other said: ""I recited the Talbiyah for Hajj like the Hajj of the Prophet ﷺ."""
"806","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from Lady Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! What is the matter with the people that they have ended their ihram after performing ‘Umrah, but you have not ended your ihram after your ‘Umrah?"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""I have stuck my hair (with gum) and put a garland on my sacrificial animal, so I will not end my ihram until I have slaughtered my sacrifice."""
"807","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Harith bin Naufal (may Allah have mercy on him) that he heard Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas and Dahhak bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with them both) discussing Hajj Tamattu’ in the year when Mu’awiyah bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) came for Hajj. Dahhak said, “Only the one who does not know the law of Allah will perform Hajj Tamattu’.” Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O nephew, you have not spoken well.” Dahhak said, “Indeed, ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade it.” So Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Hajj Tamattu’ and we also performed Hajj Tamattu’ with him.”"
"808","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Performing Umrah before Hajj and offering a sacrifice is more beloved to me than performing Umrah after Hajj in the month of Dhul-Hijjah."
"809","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked, ""What do you say about performing Umrah before Hajj, while Allah Almighty says: __QUR_N__?"" So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""How do you recite: Is the repayment of debt before the execution of the will, or is the execution of the will before the repayment of debt?"" They said, ""The execution of the will is before the repayment of debt."" He said, ""Which of the two will you begin with?"" They said, ""With the debt (i.e., we will pay the debt first)."" He said, ""So that is it."" Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: That is, it is permissible to perform Umrah before Hajj."
"810","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) intended to perform Hajj in the year of turmoil, put on the Ihram, then reflected and said: Hajj and Umrah are both the same; I make you witnesses that I have made Umrah obligatory along with Hajj."
"811","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. Among us were some who entered into the state of Ihram for Hajj, and among us were some who entered into the state of Ihram for Umrah, and among us were some who combined Hajj and Umrah. And I was among those who entered into the state of Ihram for Umrah."
"812","It is narrated from Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet ﷺ passed by Dubaa’ah bint Zubair and said: “Do you not intend to perform Hajj?” She replied, “I am doubtful because of illness.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her: “Enter into the state of Ihram for Hajj and stipulate the condition that I will become free from Ihram wherever I am prevented (due to illness).”"
"813","It is narrated from Urwah who reports that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said to me: ""When you perform Hajj, do you make an exception (istithna)?"" Urwah says: I asked, ""What should I say?"" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Say, 'O Allah, I have intended Hajj and set out for it. If You make it easy for me, then it is Hajj, and if any obstacle prevents me, then it is Umrah.'"""
"814","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that he reports from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that during the time of turmoil, he set out towards Makkah for Umrah, and said: If I am prevented from reaching the House of Allah, we will do as we did with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said, meaning: We will become lawful (out of Ihram) in the same way as we became lawful with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the year of the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah."
"815","It is narrated from Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) instructed Duba'ah and said: ""Do you not wish to perform Hajj?"" She said, ""I am doubtful due to illness."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Enter into the state of Ihram for Hajj and stipulate the condition that I will become free from Ihram wherever I am prevented (from proceeding) due to my illness."""
"816","It is narrated from Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) who says that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said to me: O nephew, when you intend to perform Hajj, do you also make an exception (istithna)? I said, what should I say? Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Say: O Allah, I have intended Hajj and have set out for it. If You make it easy for me, then it is Hajj, and if any obstacle prevents me, then it is Umrah."""
"817","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never mentioned Hajj or Umrah by name in his Talbiyah."
"818","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was: O Allah! I am present, I am present, there is no partner for You, I am present, surely all praise and blessings are for You, and the kingdom is for You, there is no partner for You. Nafi’ said that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would add these words to it: I am present, I am present, and I comply with Your worship, and (all kinds of) goodness are in Your hands. (All kinds of) desire and action are towards You. (That is, for You.)"
"819","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited this Talbiyah with Tawheed: ""Here I am, O Allah! Here I am. Here I am, You have no partner, here I am. Surely all praise and blessings are for You, and sovereignty is for You alone, You have no partner."""
"820","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he states: Among the words of Talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) were also these: ""I am present, O True Deity, I am present."""
"821","It is narrated from Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) that he states: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would express his Talbiyah as follows: “Here I am, O Allah! Here I am, here I am, You have no partner. Here I am, surely all praise and blessings are for You, and the kingdom is Yours, You have no partner.” He said this until one day, when the people were returning, it was as if these words pleased him, so he added these words to it: “Here I am, true life is the life of the Hereafter.” Ibn Jurayj said: In my opinion, this was the day of ‘Arafah."
"822","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, who reports that Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) heard one of his nephews reciting the Talbiyah, and he was saying, “O Possessor of the steps!” So Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “What steps? Indeed, He is the Possessor of the steps, but in the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), we did not recite the Talbiyah in this manner.”"
"823","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Abu Bakr Thaqafi that he asked Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) while both of them were going from Mina to Arafat in the morning, ""What would you people do on this day with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?"" Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""Some of us would be reciting Talbiyah and no one would object to him, and some would be saying Takbir and no one would object to him."""
"824","It is narrated from Saib Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to me and instructed me to command my companions or those who are with me to raise their voices when reciting the Takbeer or the Talbiyah; they intend one of these two."""
"825","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Munkadir that the Prophet ﷺ used to recite the Talbiyah frequently."
"826","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to recite the Talbiyah while riding, walking, and lying down."
"827","It is narrated from Khuzaimah bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that he narrates from the Prophet (ﷺ) that when he would finish the Talbiyah, he would ask Allah Almighty for His pleasure and for Paradise, and by means of His mercy, seek protection from Hell."
"828","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he reports: Fazl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that on the return from Muzdalifah, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made him ride behind him until Mina. The Prophet (ﷺ) continued to recite the Talbiyah until he reached the Jamarah (Aqabah) for stoning."
"829","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that Fazl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) told me that the Prophet (ﷺ) seated him behind himself from Muzdalifah to Mina, and he continued to recite Talbiyah until the stoning of Jamrah (Aqabah)."
"830","From another chain, it is narrated in the same way from the Prophet ﷺ through Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"831","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The one performing Umrah will recite the Talbiyah until he begins the Tawaf, whether he starts it on foot or without walking (while riding)."
"832","It is narrated from Mujahid that it is reported from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the one performing ‘Umrah, that he will recite the Talbiyah until he kisses the Black Stone."
"833","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The one performing Umrah will recite the Talbiyah until he begins the Tawaf, whether by touching (the Black Stone) or without touching."
"834","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Masood (may Allah be pleased with him) that after performing Tawaf of the Ka'bah during Umrah, he recited the Talbiyah at Safa."
"835","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: By ""whatever is easy from the sacrificial animal"" is meant the sacrifice of a camel or a cow."
"836","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) performed Ish'ar on the right side of the hump."
"837","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that it is reported from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he did not consider it objectionable whether the (camel's) right side was marked or the left side."
"838","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man asked the Prophet (ﷺ): ""What clothes should a person in Ihram wear?"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied: ""A person in Ihram should not wear a shirt, trousers, turbans, caps, or socks. And if someone does not have shoes, he should cut the socks below the ankles and wear them."""
"839","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him: ""What clothes should a Muhrim (one in the state of Ihram) wear?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: ""A Muhrim should not wear a shirt, nor a turban, nor a cap, nor trousers, nor socks, but whoever does not have sandals may wear socks after cutting them below the ankles."""
"840","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade a Muhrim from wearing clothes dyed with saffron or wars. He said: ""Whoever does not have shoes should wear leather socks after cutting them below the ankles."""
"841","Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying while delivering a sermon: ""When a person in Ihram does not have shoes, he should wear socks, and when he does not find an izar (waist-wrapper), he should wear trousers."""
"842","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw a man who had tied his Ihram with a colored rope. The Prophet (ﷺ) said twice: ""Remove the rope, remove the rope."""
"843","It is narrated from Muslim bin Jundab, he states that a man came and was asking Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) while I was with them. That man said: In the state of Ihram, can I take both ends of my sheet to the opposite sides behind me and tie a knot on them? Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) replied: You must not tie a knot at all."
"844","Nafi' narrated that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) did not tie a knot in the cloth he was wearing, but rather folded both its ends and tucked them inside his izar."
"845","It is narrated from Tawus who states that I saw Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) performing Tawaf of the House of Allah, and he had tied (the Ihram) around his waist with a single cloth."
"846","It is narrated from Abu Ja'far that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) saw Abdullah bin Ja'far wearing two dyed garments while in the state of ihram, so he asked: What are these garments? Ali bin Abu Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I do not consider it necessary for anyone to teach us the Sunnah. At this, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) remained silent."
"847","It is narrated from Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade any man from using saffron."
"848","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) disliked wearing a belt (waistband) for a person in the state of Ihram."
"849","It is narrated from Ya'la bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him), he states: ""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Ji'ranah when a man came to him who was wearing a cloak and was scented with khaluq. He said: O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I have entered into ihram for 'umrah and I am wearing this (cloak). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked him: What would you do regarding this in the performance of your Hajj? The man said: I would take off this cloak and wash off the khaluq. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Do as you would do in your Hajj, do the same in your 'umrah."" (That is, take off the cloak and remove the effect of the khaluq.)"
"850","It is narrated from Ya'la bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with them) that a Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and he was wearing a shirt or a cloak, and there were traces of yellow color on it. He said: ""I have entered into Ihram and I am wearing this (cloak or shirt)."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Take off your shirt or your cloak and remove this yellow color from yourself, and do in your 'Umrah as you do in your Hajj."""
"851","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel for a day and night without a mahram."""
"852","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say in a sermon: ""No man should be alone with a woman, and it is not permissible for a woman to travel except with a mahram (close male relative)."" A man stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! My name has been registered for such-and-such battle, while my wife has gone for Hajj?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Go and perform Hajj with your wife."""
"853","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that he said: Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us a hadith, and he was describing the Hajj (Farewell Pilgrimage) of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: When we reached the place of Dhul-Hulaifah, Asma bint Umays (may Allah be pleased with her) gave birth to a child, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to perform ghusl (ritual bath) and to enter into ihram."
"854","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who states: ""A woman will not wear clothes scented with perfume, and she may wear yellow-colored clothes, because in my opinion, yellow color does not have fragrance."""
"855","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: ""A woman will wear a large sheet and she will not do it in this way."" Ata says, I asked, what will she not do? So he gestured to me, in the way a woman takes a scarf. Then he indicated the scarf that is on the cheek and said: ""She will not cover her face with it, and the extra sheet will hang over her face in the way that it naturally hangs. She will neither turn it over, nor put it on, nor join it."""
"856","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he used to give the verdict to women that they should cut their socks while in Ihram. Until Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him through Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she used to give the verdict to women that they should not cut their socks. After that, Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) abandoned his verdict."
"857","It is narrated from Safiyyah bint Shaybah that she said: I was with Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) when a woman from the women of Banu Abdud-Dar came, who was called Tamlik. She said: ""O Mother of the Believers! My such-and-such daughter has sworn an oath that she will not wear her jewelry during the (Hajj) season."" So Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Tell her that the Mother of the Believers adjures her by oath to wear all her jewelry."""
"858","Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabee’ah said that I was a companion of Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), and I did not see him use a tent during Hajj until he returned."
"859","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came during the compensatory ‘Umrah with swords hanging (by their sides) while they were in the state of Ihram."
"860","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Haneen that Abdullah bin Abbas and Miswar bin Makhrama (may Allah be pleased with them) had a disagreement at a place called Abwa. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""A person in the state of Ihram can wash his head,"" while Miswar said, ""A person in the state of Ihram cannot wash his head."" So Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) sent me to Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) to ask about the matter. When I arrived, he was bathing between two wooden beams of a well, having covered himself with a cloth. When I arrived and greeted him with salam, he asked, ""Who are you?"" I replied, ""I am Abdullah, and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) has sent me to you to ask how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to wash his blessed head while in the state of Ihram."" Upon hearing this, he placed his hand on the cloth (with which he had covered himself) and lowered it until I could see his head. Then he told the person who was pouring water over his body to pour water over his head. That person poured water over his head, then he washed his head with both hands, moving both hands forward and then backward, and then said, ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do it in this manner while in the state of Ihram."""
"861","It is narrated from Ya'la bin Umayyah that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was performing ghusl behind a camel and I was holding a cloth as a screen for him, when Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Ya'la! Pour water over my head."" So I said: ""Ameer al-Mu'mineen knows best."" Then Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""By Allah! Water only increases the hair in disarray."" Then he mentioned the name of Allah and poured water over his head."
"862","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Sometimes Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Come, let me dip you in the water so that we may see whose breath lasts longer,"" and we were in the state of Ihram."
"863","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he entered the bathhouse at the place of Juhfa while in the state of Ihram and said: ""Allah Almighty does not care at all about our dirt and filth."""
"864","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that when he suffered from eye inflammation while in the state of Ihram, he would put drops of aloe in his eyes, and he said: ""A Muhrim may apply any kind of kohl for eye inflammation except for perfumed kohl, for that is not permissible even in a normal state without the illness of eye inflammation."""
"865","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked: ""Can a person in Ihram smell basil (fragrant herb), oil, and perfume?"" He replied: ""No."""
"866","It is narrated from Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person in the state of ihram should neither marry nor arrange a marriage."""
"867","It is narrated from Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person in the state of Ihram should neither marry, nor arrange a marriage, nor propose."""
"868","It is narrated from Nabiya bin Wahb that Umar bin Ubaidullah intended to marry Talha bin Umar to the daughter of Shaibah bin Jubair, so he sent a message to Aban bin Uthman to participate (in the marriage), and both (the ones to be married) were in the state of ihram. Aban refused to participate and said: I heard Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Neither should a person in ihram marry, nor arrange a marriage, nor propose."""
"869","Through another chain from Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), a hadith with similar meaning to the previous hadith is narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"870","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: ""A person in the state of Ihram should neither marry, nor arrange a marriage for someone else, nor propose, nor arrange a proposal for someone else."""
"871","It is narrated from Abu Ghatfan bin Tarif Al-Mari that he reported his father Tarif married a woman while in the state of Ihram, so Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) annulled their marriage."
"872","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent his servant Abu Rafi' and two men from the Ansar, so they married him to Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), and the Prophet (ﷺ) was in Medina."
"873","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib, may Allah have mercy on him, that he said: ""So-and-so was mistaken because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married Maymunah while he was in a state of being lawful (not in ihram)."""
"874","It is narrated from Yazid bin Asam (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while he was in a state of being lawful (not in Ihram)."
"875","It is narrated from Sulayman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent Abu Rafi‘ (who was his servant) and a man from the Ansar, so they married him to Maymunah bint al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) before he left Madinah (for Makkah)."
"876","It is narrated from Yazid bin Asam (may Allah have mercy on him) (he is the nephew of Maymunah, may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in a state of being lawful (not in Ihram)."
"877","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: ""He is mistaken who stated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married Maymunah while in the state of ihram; the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married her while he was not in ihram."""
"878","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: ""I asked Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) about the statement of Allah: 'Do not kill game while you are in the state of Ihram, and whoever among you kills it intentionally...' (__QUR_N__ Al-Ma'idah: 95) — Is there also a penalty for the one who kills unintentionally?"" Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""Yes, this is out of reverence for the sanctities of Allah, and this is how it has been practiced."""
"879","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: ""I saw that people would give blood money (diyah) even in cases of accidental killing of an animal."""
"880","Ibn Jurayj said: Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) used to say that whoever among you (hunts) deliberately kills (the game) without forgetting, while in the state of ihram, and he has no other intention besides this, then he has made a mistake and it has become lawful, and there is no concession for him; and whoever kills it without remembering its sanctity or had some other intention besides this, then he has also made a mistake. This (mistaken) intention is such that for it, there is expiation with an animal of its like."
"881","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata (may Allah have mercy on him): ""And the compensation is obligatory, equivalent to the animal which he has killed, as judged by two just men among you (whether that compensation is from the cattle), to be brought as an offering to the Ka'bah, or as an expiation, to feed the needy."" (Al-Ma'idah: 95) Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Because he hunted that animal in the Haram and he also intends the House of Allah, so its expiation must also be given near the House of Allah."
"882","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar regarding Allah's command: ""There is a ransom, so he may fast, or give charity, or offer a sacrifice."" (__QUR_N__: Al-Baqarah: 196) that there is a choice in this; he may do whichever he wishes."
"883","It is narrated from Ata that he heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) say: For a badger, the compensation is a ram."
"884","Ikrimah—the freed slave of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them)—narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) hunted a badger with a small spear, and for its compensation, he decreed a ram."
"885","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the verdict of a goat as compensation in the case of hunting a young deer."
"886","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that for a hare, a one-year-old lamb or kid should be given, and for killing a jerboa, a four-month-old kid should be given as compensation."
"887","It is narrated from Tariq bin Shihab who said: ""We set out for Hajj, and one of us, whose name was Arbad, hunted a deer and wounded its back. We came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and Arbad asked him about it. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Arbad, you yourself decide (what compensation you should give).' He said: 'O Commander of the Faithful! You are more knowledgeable and better than me.' Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: 'I order you to decide in this matter; I did not order you to describe my qualities.' So Arbad said: 'In my opinion, its compensation is a goat that is fit for grazing.' Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said (confirming): 'That is its compensation.'"""
"888","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) issued the ruling that as compensation: for a badger, a ram; for a young deer, a goat; for a rabbit, a one-year-old lamb or kid; and for a jerboa, a four-month-old kid should be given."
"889","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he gave the verdict of giving a four-month-old goat kid in (the tribe of) Yarbu'."
"890","It is narrated from Abu Safar that Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that as compensation for killing an animal resembling a lizard, a kid from the goats should be given."
"891","It is narrated from Ziyad, who was a freed slave of Banu Makhzum and was trustworthy: A group of people hunted while in the state of Ihram, so Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to them: ""A penalty (fidyah) is obligatory upon you."" They asked: ""Is a separate penalty obligatory upon each one of us, or is there only one for all of us?"" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) replied: ""Not as it is commonly known among you, rather only one penalty is obligatory upon all of you."""
"892","It is narrated from Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said regarding the egg of an ostrich: ""Whoever in the state of Ihram picks it up, then there is a compensation of fasting for one day or feeding one needy person upon him."""
"893","It is also narrated in a similar manner from Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission."
"894","It is narrated from Yusuf bin Mahak that Abdullah bin Abi Ammar told him that he came with Mu'adh bin Jabal and Ka'b al-Ahbar (may Allah be pleased with them both) among the people in the state of ihram for 'Umrah from Bayt al-Maqdis. When we were on the way and Ka'b was warming himself by a fire, a swarm of locusts passed by him, so he caught two locusts and roasted them, forgetting that he was in ihram. Then, when he remembered that he was in ihram, he threw them away. When we came to Madinah, the people went to 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and I also went. Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) related the incident of the locusts to 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""Who is that? Perhaps, O Ka'b, it is you?"" Ka'b said: ""Yes."" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Indeed, Himyar (an ancient tribe of Yemen) likes locusts."" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""How much fidyah (compensation) have you calculated for yourself?"" He replied: ""Two dirhams."" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Wow! Two dirhams are better than a hundred locusts, so keep what you have calculated for yourself."""
"895","Ata says that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked about hunting locusts in the Haram, so he replied: ""No,"" and forbade it. Ata said: I said to him, or a man from the people said to him, ""Your people sit in the mosque tied up with their clothes, and they catch them?"" So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""They do not have knowledge."""
"896","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain in the same manner, but in this narration, the narrator has mentioned the words «منحنون» (that they are bent) instead of «محتبون» . And the memorizers have narrated from Ibn Jurayj that «منحنون» is more eloquent than «محتبون» ."
"897","Qasim narrates that I was sitting with Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) when a man asked him about the ruling of killing a locust while in the state of Ihram. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""For this, a handful of food (as compensation) is required, and he should definitely catch a handful of locusts."" Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) says that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas’s statement that he should catch a handful of locusts means that only the value will be considered, and his saying «ولو» means that caution will be exercised in paying that value, and he will give more than what is obligatory upon him, after I have informed you that it is more than what is obligatory upon you."
"898","Bukair bin Abdullah narrates from Qasim that a man asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) about a muhrim (person in the state of ihram) who hunts locusts. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that he should give a handful of grain as charity. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) also said that he should take a handful of locusts, but this is an opinion (i.e., there is no Shari' evidence for it)."
"899","It is narrated from Nafi' bin 'Abd al-Harith: He said, Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Makkah and on Friday entered Dar al-Nadwah. He intended to go to the mosque from nearby. He placed his cloak on something standing in the house. Then one of the pigeons came and sat on it. He shooed it away, and a snake pounced on it and killed it. After performing the Friday prayer, I and Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) came to him. He said: ""Both of you decide about a matter I did today. I came to this house and intended to go to the mosque from nearby. I placed my cloak on that standing thing, and one of the pigeons came and sat on it. I was afraid it might soil it with its droppings, so I shooed it away. It went and sat on another standing thing, and a snake pounced on it and killed it. I became worried that I had driven it away from a place of safety, and it went and sat in a place where it was killed."" Nafi' says, I said to Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him): ""What do you think about the two-toothed goat, should we tell the Commander of the Faithful to pay its compensation?"" He said: ""That is also my opinion."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered its compensation to be paid."
"900","It is narrated from Ata that the son of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Humaid killed a pigeon. He came to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) and mentioned this matter to him, so Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""Slaughter a goat and give it in charity."" Ibn Jurayj said: I asked Ata, ""Was it from the pigeons of Makkah?"" He replied, ""Yes."""
"901","It is narrated from Ata that a slave of the Quraysh killed a female pigeon from among the pigeons of Makkah, so Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered that a goat be given as compensation on his behalf."
"902","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The meat of game is lawful for you in the state of Ihram as long as you do not hunt it yourselves or it is not hunted for you."""
"903","It is also narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through another chain in this manner."
"904","From another chain of narration, it is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ) in this manner."
"905","Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, said that Ibn Abi Yahya has better memorization than Darawardi and Sulayman ibn Abi Yahya."
"906","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from Sa'b bin Jaththamah (may Allah be pleased with him), that when they were at Abwa or Waddan, he presented a wild donkey as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned it. Then, when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw displeasure on his face, he said: ""If we were not in the state of Ihram, we would not have returned it to you."""
"907","It is narrated from Abu Qatadah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was with the Prophet ﷺ on the way to Makkah. He, along with some of his companions who were in the state of Ihram, stayed behind, while he himself (Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him) was not in Ihram. He saw a wild donkey and mounted his horse. Then he said to his companions (who were in Ihram), ""Hand me the whip,"" but they refused. Then he asked for his spear, but they also refused to give it. Finally, he took his own spear, attacked the donkey, and killed it. Some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ ate its meat, while others refused (because of being in Ihram). When they reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they asked him about this issue. He ﷺ said: ""This was a meal which Allah provided for you."""
"908","The incident of the wild donkey narrated by Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) through the authority of Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) is also reported similar to the hadith of Abu al-Nadr."
"909","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi'ah who said: I saw Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) at the place of 'Arj during the hot days, in the state of Ihram, and he had covered his face with a red sheet. Then some game meat was brought to him, so he said to his companions, ""You eat!"" They asked, ""Will you not eat?"" Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, ""I am not like you, because this game was hunted for me."""
"910","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""There are five animals which it is not sinful for a person in the state of Ihram to kill: the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, and the biting dog."""
"911","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Ammar: He said, I saw Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) at the place of Baida, in the state of Ihram, shooting a crow with an arrow."
"912","It is narrated from Rabi'ah bin Abdullah bin Hudair that he saw Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) at the place of Suqya, in the state of Ihram, removing ticks from his camel and throwing them into the dust."
"913","Maimun bin Mehran narrated that I was with Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) when a man asked him: ""I caught a louse and dropped it, then searched for it but could not find it."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""This is a lost thing for which there is no need to search."""
"914","It is narrated from Maymun bin Mehran, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) when a man came and sat down. I had not seen a man with longer hair than him. He said: I have entered into Ihram while having this hair. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Tie up the hair above your ears. The man then said: I kissed a woman other than my wife. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Your mouth has committed adultery."" The man then said: I saw a louse and threw it away. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""This is such a lost thing that there is no benefit in searching for it."""
"915","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (ﷺ) had cupping done while in the state of Ihram."
"916","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) had cupping done while in the state of Ihram."
"917","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to say: A Muhrim should not get cupped unless there is such a necessity for which there is no alternative."
"918","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saw a mirror while he was in the state of Ihram."
"919","It is narrated from Hasan bin Qasim Al-Azraqi that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was riding his she-camel in the state of Ihram, and the camel began to act up, stepping forward with one foot and backward with the other. Rabi’ said: In my opinion, these verses were recited by Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): It is as if the rider of this she-camel is like those branches that sway like a swing in strong winds, or its rider is like a drinker who is intoxicated with wine. Then he said: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest."
"920","It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Aswad bin Abd Yaghuth that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Indeed, there is wisdom in some poetry."""
"921","Hisham bin Urwah narrates from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Poetry is (a form of) speech; its beauty is like the beauty of speech, and its ugliness is like the ugliness of speech."""
"922","It is narrated from Zaid bin Jubair that he said: ""I was with Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) when he was asked about this, so he said: This is the Hajj of Islam; he should fulfill his vow."" That is, the one upon whom Hajj is obligatory and he has made a vow to perform Hajj."
"923","It is narrated from Ata that he said: The Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying, ""I am present on behalf of so-and-so."" So the Prophet ﷺ said to him: ""If you have performed Hajj before, then recite the Talbiyah on his behalf; if not, then first perform Hajj for yourself, then fulfill it on his behalf."""
"924","It is narrated from Ata who reports that the Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying: ""I am present on behalf of so-and-so."" So the Prophet ﷺ said: ""If you have performed Hajj before, then say Labbaik on his behalf, and if not, then first perform Hajj for yourself."""
"925","It is narrated from Abu Qilabah: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) heard a man saying, ""I am present on behalf of Shubrumah."" So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""You are ruined! What is this Shubrumah?"" The man explained his relationship to Shubrumah. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) asked, ""Have you performed Hajj for yourself first?"" He said, ""No."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""First perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah."""
"926","It is narrated from Abu Qilabah that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard a man saying: ""I am present on behalf of Shubrumah."" So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Woe to you! Who is this Shubrumah?"" One of Ayyub and Khalid al-Hadha said that the man replied: ""He is my brother."" The other said that he mentioned his relationship to Shubrumah. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Have you performed Hajj on your own behalf?"" He replied: ""No."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Perform Hajj on your own behalf first, then (afterwards) perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah."""
"927","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a woman from the tribe of Khath'am asked the Prophet ﷺ a question. She said: ""The obligation of Hajj, which Allah has made upon His servants, has reached my elderly father, but he does not have the strength to sit on a mount. What do you think—can I perform Hajj on his behalf?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied: ""Yes."" Sufyan said: I have remembered it from Zuhri in this way."
"928","It is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through the chain of Amr bin Dinar in a similar manner, and in this narration, these additional words are mentioned: That woman said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Will this (Hajj on behalf of another) benefit him?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied, ""Yes, just as if he had a debt and you paid it off on his behalf, it would benefit him; in the same way, Hajj will also benefit him."""
"929","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he stated: Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on his mount. A woman from the tribe of Khath'am came and began to ask for a religious ruling. Fadl started looking at her and she started looking at Fadl. So the Prophet (ﷺ) turned Fadl's face to the other side. The woman said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Allah's obligation of Hajj has reached my elderly father in such a state that he cannot sit on a mount. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?"" He (ﷺ) said: ""Yes."" And this was during the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"930","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a woman from the tribe of Khath'am said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): ""Allah's obligation of Hajj has reached my father while he is very old and cannot sit on the back of his camel."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Perform Hajj on his behalf."""
"931","It is narrated from Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""All of Mina is a place for sacrifice."" Then a woman from the tribe of Khath'am came to him and said: ""My father has become old and weak, and the obligation of Hajj, which Allah has made upon His servants, has reached him, but he does not have the strength to perform it. If I perform it on his behalf, will it suffice for him?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Yes."""
"932","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""My mother has passed away and Hajj was obligatory upon her."" So the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Perform Hajj on behalf of your mother."""
"933","It is narrated from Ibn Sirin, may Allah have mercy on him, that a man made a vow that when any of his children reached the age of weaning—such that he would wash milk, drink it himself, and give it to those with him—he would take him along and perform Hajj himself as well. One of the old man’s children came to know of this, and that man had become very old. So his son told the whole matter to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Indeed, my father has become very old, he does not have the strength to perform Hajj. Can I perform Hajj (as a substitute) on his behalf?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yes.”"
"934","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! My mother is very old, she does not have the strength to ride on a camel, and if I tie her on, I fear she may die. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Yes."""
"935","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that a man asked him: ""I have taken employment with a people (on the condition that) I will perform Hajj with them, so will my Hajj be valid?"" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""Yes, these are the people for whom there is a share in what they earn, and Allah is swift in taking account."" (__QUR_2:202__)"
"936","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that a man asked Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): ""I have taken employment with a people so that I will perform Hajj with them. Will my Hajj be valid?"" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""Yes, for them is their share of deeds, and Allah is swift in taking account."""
"937","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Prophet ﷺ returned and met some riders at the place of Rauha, he ﷺ greeted them with salam and asked: ""Who are you people?"" They replied: ""We are Muslims, and who are you people?"" He ﷺ said: ""I am the Messenger of Allah."" A woman lifted her child in her hands from the litter and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there Hajj (valid) for this child?"" He ﷺ replied: ""Yes, and the reward is for you."""
"938","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed by a woman who was in a litter. It was said to her: ""This is the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" She took hold of her child's arm and said: ""Is his Hajj valid?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes, and the reward is for you."""
"939","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed by a woman who was in a palanquin. It was said to the woman: ""This is the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" She took hold of her child's arm and said: ""Is his Hajj valid?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""Yes, and the reward is for you."""
"940","Abu As-Safar narrated that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""O people! Let me hear what you say, and understand what I say to you: If a slave is made to perform Hajj by his masters and he dies before being freed, then his Hajj is complete. But if he is freed before dying, then he should perform Hajj (again). And if a child is made to perform Hajj by his family and he dies before Hajj becomes obligatory upon him, then his Hajj is complete. But if he reaches maturity, then he should perform Hajj (again)."""
"941","Abu As-Safar narrated that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""O people! Let me hear what you say, and understand what I say to you! If a slave is made to perform Hajj by his masters and he dies before being freed, then his Hajj is complete. But if he is freed before dying, then he should (perform Hajj) again. And if a child is made to perform Hajj by his family and he dies before Hajj becomes obligatory upon him, then his Hajj is complete, and if he reaches maturity, then he should (perform Hajj) again."""
"942","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""There is no impediment (ihsar) except the enemy."" One of Ibn Tawus and Amr bin Dinar narrated these additional words: ""Now even that (enemy's) impediment has ended."""
"943","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""Whoever is prevented (due to illness), he should not exit the state of Ihram until he has performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah and the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah."""
"944","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: ""Whoever is prevented from the House of Allah due to illness should not exit the state of Ihram until he has performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah and the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah."""
"945","It is narrated from Sulayman bin Yasar that Ibn Umar, Marwan, and Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them) gave a fatwa to Ibn Khuzamah al-Makhzumi, while he was afflicted with a headache on the way to Makkah and was also in the state of ihram. They said that he should seek treatment as much as possible, and gave him the fatwa that when he becomes healthy, he should perform ‘umrah and come out of ihram. Now it is obligatory upon him that he perform Hajj the following year and also offer a sacrifice."
"946","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to perform ghusl (ritual bath) before entering Makkah."
"947","It is narrated from Ata that he said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah, he neither turned towards anyone nor inclined towards anyone."
"948","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see the House of Allah, he would raise both his hands and supplicate: ""O Allah! Increase the honor, greatness, nobility, and awe of this House, and increase the honor, dignity, greatness, and goodness of those among the people who honored and ennobled it, those who performed Hajj and ‘Umrah of it."""
"949","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib that when he would see the House of Allah, he would recite this supplication: ""O Allah! You are the Source of peace and from You is all peace, so O Lord, keep us alive with peace."""
"950","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""The hands should be raised in prayer, and when seeing the Ka'bah, then at Safa and Marwah, on the night of Arafah, at Muzdalifah, near the two Jamrahs, and over the deceased."""
"951","Muhammad bin Abbad bin Ja'far narrated that I saw Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) come to the Black Stone, and his head was dusty. He kissed it, then prostrated on it, then kissed it and prostrated on it, then kissed it and prostrated on it."
"952","It is narrated from Abu Ja'far that he said: I saw Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) come to (Makkah) on the eighth of Dhul-Hijjah, his head covered with dust. He kissed the Black Stone, then prostrated on it, then kissed it and prostrated on it, and did this three times."
"953","Ibn Jurayj narrated that I asked Ata: ""Have you seen any of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), may Allah be pleased with them, kiss their hands when they performed istilam?"" Ata said: ""Yes, I saw Jabir bin Abdullah, Ibn Umar, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with them, that when they performed istilam, they also kissed their hands."" Ibn Jurayj said: ""And Ibn Abbas as well?"" Ata said: ""Yes, and I think I saw many more."" Ibn Jurayj said: ""Do you not kiss your hands when you perform istilam?"" He said: ""(Yes,) but now I do not kiss them."""
"954","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: When you find a crowd at the Rukn (Hajar al-Aswad), then turn back; do not stand there."
"955","Manbuz bin Abi Sulaiman narrates from his mother that she was with the Prophet’s ﷺ wife Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) when her freed slave woman came to her and said: “O Mother of the Believers! I performed seven circuits of the House of Allah and touched (the Black Stone) two or three times.” So Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said to her: “May Allah not reward you, may Allah not reward you! Were you pushing away the men? Could you not have just passed by saying takbir?”"
"956","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Tawaf during Hajj and Umrah, he would run during the first three circuits and walk during the remaining four, then he would pray two rak'ahs, and then perform the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah."
"957","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) completed three out of the seven circuits by walking briskly (performing ramal), and there was no walking at a normal pace in between them."
"958","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he would perform raml from the Black Stone to the Black Stone, then he would say: ""This is how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did."""
"959","It is narrated from Masruq (may Allah have mercy on him) that he saw Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) begin by touching the Black Stone, then perform three circuits (tawaf) on the right side with a brisk walk (raml), and four circuits with a normal walk. Then he came to the Station of Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and offered two rak'ahs of prayer behind it."
"960","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Mulaykah that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) touched the Black Stone in order to perform Tawaf, then said: ""Now, for whom should we expose our shoulders, and to whom should we show (our strength), when Allah has made Islam dominant? By Allah! I will perform Sa'i (Tawaf) in the same manner as they (i.e., the Prophet ﷺ) did."""
"961","Tawoos says: I heard Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) saying: ""Speak little during Tawaf, for you are in worship like prayer."""
"962","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: ""I performed Tawaf behind Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), and I did not hear any of them speak until they had completed their Tawaf."""
"963","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ka'b (may Allah have mercy on him) that one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to touch all the corners and would say: ""It is not permissible to leave out anything from the House of Allah."" So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Indeed, for you in the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) is the best example."" (__QUR_N__: Al-Ahzab: 21)"
"964","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ka'b (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to touch the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone, while Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) used to touch all the corners and would say: ""Nothing from the House of Allah should be left out."" And Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) would say: ""Indeed, for you in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is the best example."" (__QUR_33_21__)"
"965","It is narrated from Sa’ib bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicating between the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone: “Our Lord! Grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of the Fire.” (__QUR_2:201__)"
"966","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""Hijr (i.e., Hatim) is a part of the House of Allah, and Allah Almighty has said: 'And let them circumambulate the Ancient House of Allah.' (__QUR_N__: Al-Hajj: 29) And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Tawaf from behind the Hijr (Hatim)."""
"967","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know that when your people rebuilt the Ka'bah, they left out the foundation of Ibrahim (peace be upon him)?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Why do you not rebuild it upon the foundation of Ibrahim (peace be upon him)?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If your people were not so close to the time of disbelief, I would have rebuilt it upon its original foundation."" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""If Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (and indeed Aisha did hear it), then I think this is the reason why the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not kiss the two corners adjacent to the Hatim, because the House of Allah was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."""
"968","Abu Yazid narrated that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a man to an old man from Banu Zuhrah, so I also came with him to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he was in Hatim. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked him about the children of the pre-Islamic period of ignorance, so the old man said: ""The semen would be from one person, and the child would be born on the bed of another."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You have spoken the truth, but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decided that the child belongs to the owner of the bed."" When the old man turned back, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) called him and asked: ""Tell me about the construction of the House of Allah (the Ka'bah)?"" He said: ""The Quraysh collected donations for the construction of the Ka'bah, but they were unable to complete it, so they left some of its part in the Hatim."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""You have spoken the truth."""
"969","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Tawaf of the House (Ka'bah) and the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah during the Farewell Pilgrimage while riding his camel, so that people could see him and so that he would be above them, because the people had surrounded him."
"970","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the circumambulation of the Ka'bah on his camel, and touched the Black Stone with his staff."
"971","From another chain of narration, it is reported from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the Prophet ﷺ in the same manner."
"972","Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah and the Sa’i between Safa and Marwah while riding. Ibn Jurayj says: I asked, “Why?” Ata said: “I do not know.” He said: “Then the Prophet (ﷺ) dismounted and prayed two rak’ahs (at the Station of Ibrahim).”"
"973","Ahwas bin Hakim narrated that I saw Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) performing Sa'i between Safa and Marwah while riding a donkey."
"974","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) performed Tawaf of the Ka'bah while riding his camel, and he would touch the Black Stone with his staff."
"975","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): ""Your (one) Tawaf of the House of Allah and (one) Sa'i between Safa and Marwah are sufficient for your Hajj and Umrah."""
"976","From another chain of narration, it is reported from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a similar manner."
"977","Sometimes Sufyan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) without the intermediary of Ibn Abi Najih (may Allah have mercy on him), and he (Ata) narrates from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"978","And sometimes these words were said: The Prophet ﷺ said to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"979","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah and the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah in all four of his Umrahs, except that in the first and fourth Umrah, they turned him back from Hudaybiyyah."
"980","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) for Hajj, he performed Sa'i, then during his own caliphate Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) also did so, then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), then Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), and the caliphs who came after them—all the caliphs after them used to perform Sa'i in the same manner."""
"981","Safiyyah bint Shaybah narrates: ""A woman from Banu Abdud-Dar, the daughter of Abi Tijarah, told me that I came with the women of Quraysh to the house of Abi Al-Husayn, and we were watching the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. I saw him performing Sa'i, and his lower garment was twisting due to the intensity of the Sa'i, to the extent that I say I saw his knees. And I heard him saying: 'Perform Sa'i! Indeed, Allah has made Sa'i obligatory upon you.'"""
"982","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: There is neither Sa'i of the House of Allah upon women, nor of Safa and Marwah."
"983","It is narrated from Hasan bin Muslim bin Yanaq: He said, during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Day of Tarwiyah (the 8th of Dhul-Hijjah) fell on a Friday. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in front of the Ka'bah and instructed the people to proceed towards Mina, and he ﷺ himself also went and performed the Zuhr prayer in Mina."
"984","Salim narrates from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed two rak‘ahs in Mina, and afterwards Abu Bakr and ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) did the same."
"985","It is narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"986","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the sun would rise, he would depart from Mina to Arafat in the morning."
"987","Amr bin Dinar narrates that the person who saw Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) told me that he used to come to the place of Arafah at the time of Suhoor."
"988","Zadhan narrated that a man asked Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about ghusl (ritual bath), so he replied, ""If you wish, perform ghusl every day."" The man asked, ""The ghusl that is obligatory?"" Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, ""On the day of Jumu'ah (Friday), the day of Arafah, the day of sacrifice (Eid al-Adha), and the day of Eid al-Fitr."""
"989","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated regarding the Hajj of Islam that the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to the place of standing at Arafat, delivered the first sermon to the people, then Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) called the adhan, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) began the second sermon. When he (peace be upon him) finished his sermon, Bilal had finished the adhan. Then Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the iqamah and the Zuhr prayer was performed, then Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the iqamah and the Asr prayer was performed."
"990","It is narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them). Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The statement that I make is this: At Arafah, there is one adhan and two iqamahs."
"991","The same hadith is narrated through another chain from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), in a similar manner."
"992","Yazid bin Shaiban said, We were standing at Arafat. Amr described this place as being very far from the place where the Imam stays. Ibn Muraqqa’ Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us and said, I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to remain at your respective places, because you are inheritors of a legacy from your father Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"993","Nafi’ (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: Whoever among the pilgrims reaches the night of sacrifice while staying at the mountains of ‘Arafah before the break of dawn, he has attained the Hajj. And whoever does not reach ‘Arafah, but stays there until before the break of dawn, his Hajj is missed. He should come to the House of Allah, perform seven circuits (Tawaf) around it, and perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwah for seven rounds. Then, if he wishes, he may shave his head or shorten his hair. And if he has a sacrificial animal, he should slaughter it before shaving his head. And when he has completed the Tawaf and Sa’i, he should shave or shorten his hair. Then he should return to his home. If in the coming year he attains Hajj and has the means, he should perform Hajj and also offer a sacrifice. If he cannot find a sacrificial animal, then in its place he should fast three days during the days of Hajj and seven when he returns home."
"994","Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) set out for Hajj, and on the way to Makkah, at the place of Badiyah, his camel was lost. He came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day of sacrifice and informed him of this matter. So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him, ""Do as those performing ‘Umrah do, then come out of Ihram. Then, when you reach Hajj in the coming year, perform Hajj and offer as sacrifice whatever is available from the Hadi."""
"995","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that Habar bin Aswad came while Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was slaughtering a she-camel."
"996","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Qais bin Makhramah that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and said: ""The people of ignorance used to return from Arafat before the sun had set, and from Muzdalifah after the sun had risen, to the extent that the sun would appear as if turbans were on the faces of the people. But we will not return from Arafat until the sun has set, and from Muzdalifah we will depart before the sun rises. Our way is contrary to that of the polytheists and idol worshippers."""
"997","It is narrated from Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: In the days of ignorance, people would return from Arafat before the sun had set and from Muzdalifah after the sun had risen, and they would say: ""O Thabir (the name of a mountain), shine so that we may return."" So Allah the Exalted delayed (the departure from Arafat) until sunset and made (the departure from Muzdalifah) earlier (i.e., before sunrise)."
"998","It is also narrated in a similar manner through another chain."
"999","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Qais bin Makhramah that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""In the days of ignorance, people would return from Arafah before the sun set and from Muzdalifah after the sun had risen, and they would say: 'O Thabir, shine so we may return.' Allah has postponed one and advanced the other; that is, He made Muzdalifah earlier, up to before sunrise, and Arafah later, up to sunset."""
"1000","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) combined the Maghrib and Isha prayers at Muzdalifah and offered them together."
"1001","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""I was among those whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent from Muzdalifah to Mina along with the weak people of his household."""
"1002","Hisham bin Urwah narrates from his father that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) on the Day of Nahr (the day of sacrifice) and instructed her to hasten from Muzdalifah for the Tawaf al-Ifadah. So she came to Makkah and performed the Fajr prayer there. And it was the day of Umm Salamah’s turn, and the Prophet ﷺ liked that she should join him."
"1003","It is narrated in a similar manner from the Prophet ﷺ through another chain from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1004","It is narrated from Umrah bint Abd al-Rahman that she stated: When women performed Hajj with Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and they feared the onset of menstruation, Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) would send them ahead on the Day of Sacrifice, and they would perform the Tawaf al-Ifadah. And if they menstruated after that, she would not give them time to become pure, rather she would depart with them (from Mecca) while they were in a state of menstruation."
"1005","It is narrated from Qasim bin Muhammad that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to instruct women to perform the Tawaf al-Ifadah early due to the fear of menstruation."
"1006","It is narrated from Tawus that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed his companions to hasten the Tawaf al-Ifadah, and he himself performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah at night among his wives on his mount. He ﷺ would touch the Black Stone with his staff. The narrator says: ""I think he also said that then he would kiss the end of the staff."""
"1007","It is narrated from Tawus that the Prophet ﷺ instructed his companions to perform the Tawaf al-Ifadah quickly, and he ﷺ himself performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah with his wives. When he performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah, he would touch the Black Stone with his staff; the narrator says: ""I think he said, and he would kiss the end of the staff."""
"1008","It is narrated from Tawus that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Muzdalifah and did not hasten his camel until he had stoned the Jamrah."
"1009","It is narrated from Jubair bin Huwairith: ""I saw Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) standing on the Qazah mountain, and he was saying: O people! Let there be full daylight. Then he departed from there, and it is as if I am looking at his thigh, with which he was striking his camel like a stick."""
"1010","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission."
"1011","It is narrated from Abu Al-Huwairith: ""I saw Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) standing on the Qazah mountain, and he was saying: O people! Let the morning become clear. Then he returned, and I saw his thigh with which he was striking his camel like a stick."""
"1012","Hisham bin Urwah narrates from his father that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was urging his camel forward quickly in the Valley of Muhassir while reciting this verse: ""Its saddle is coming towards You in restlessness. Its religion is contrary to the religion of the Christians."""
"1013","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Harith Taimi, who reports from a man of his tribe Banu Taim, whose name is Mu'adh or Ibn Mu'adh, that the Prophet ﷺ, while settling people in their places at Mina, said: ""Throw the pebbles like they are thrown with the finger."""
"1014","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw the Prophet (ﷺ) throw pebbles at the Jamarat in the manner that they are thrown with the fingers."
"1015","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar (may Allah have mercy on him) that a barber told me that he cut the hair of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), so he said: ""Start from the right side."""
"1016","Abu Ali Al-Azdi narrated that I heard Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying to the one shaving his head: O boy, shave till the bone, and when you cut the hair, start from the right side before the left side."
"1017","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when he would shave his head during Hajj or Umrah, he would also have some hair cut from his beard and mustache."
"1018","Narrated from Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was standing for the people at Mina during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and people were asking him questions. A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I did not know and I shaved my head before sacrificing, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Now offer the sacrifice, there is no harm.' Another man came and said: O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I sacrificed before stoning the Jamarat and I did not realize, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Now stone (the Jamarat), there is no harm.' Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As said: Whatever matter was asked of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding doing something before or after its due time, he (ﷺ) said: 'Now do it, there is no harm.'"""
"1019","Salim bin Abdullah narrated that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""When you have performed the stoning of the Jamarat, then everything that was made unlawful for you (due to Ihram) has now become lawful for you, except women and perfume."""
"1020","Salim bin Abdullah narrated that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""I myself applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" She said that it is in the Book of Al-Imla that (I applied perfume) for his being lawful and for Ihram. Salim said: ""And the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is more deserving to be followed."""
"1021","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: ""I applied perfume with my own hands to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for his becoming lawful (after Ihram) and for entering into Ihram during the Farewell Pilgrimage."""
"1022","It is narrated from Salim bin Abdullah that he reported from Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he forbade the use of perfume before visiting the House (Ka'bah) and after the stoning of the Jamarat. Then Salim said that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""I applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with my own hands for Ihram, before entering into Ihram, and before performing the Tawaf of the House, for being in a state of permissibility. And following the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is more deserving."""
"1023","Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""When you have stoned the Jamarat, slaughtered the animal, and shaved your head, then everything that was forbidden to you has become lawful for you except women and perfume."" Salim said that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I myself applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for Ihram before he entered into Ihram, and after stoning the Jamarat, before visiting the House of Allah, when he became lawful again. Salim said that the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) is more deserving to be followed."
"1024","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) granted permission to those among his household who provided water to spend the nights of Mina in Mecca."
"1025","It is narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Ata, except that Ata has added these words: ""Because of her giving water to drink."""
"1026","Amr bin Salim Al-Zurqi narrates from his mother that she said: ""We were in Mina when Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) was riding a camel, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed, these are days of eating and drinking; none of you should fast.' The people followed him (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was riding the camel, proclaiming this statement loudly among them."""
"1027","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding the one performing Hajj Tamattu' that if he does not have an animal for sacrifice and has not fasted before 'Arafah, then he should fast during the days of Mina (the days of Tashreeq)."
"1028","It is also narrated in a similar manner from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) through another chain from Salim."
"1029","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: When people would finish Hajj, they would depart in every direction, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""None of the pilgrims should leave until his last act is at the House of Allah (i.e., he performs the Farewell Tawaf)."""
"1030","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""None among the pilgrims should return until his last act is performed at the House of Allah. Indeed, the final act of Hajj is the (farewell) Tawaf of the House of Allah."""
"1031","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""None of the pilgrims should return until he has performed the Tawaf of the House (Ka'bah), because the last act of Hajj is the (farewell) Tawaf of the House of Allah."" Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) said: In our opinion—and Allah knows best—this is the explanation of Allah's statement: ""Then its being made lawful is at the House of Allah,"" meaning that becoming lawful from the rites of Hajj and their completion is at the Ka'bah."
"1032","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: (After performing Hajj) people would return from every direction, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should return until his last act is the circumambulation of the House (Ka'bah)."""
"1033","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The people were commanded that their last act should be the circumambulation (Tawaf) of the House (Ka'bah), except that the Prophet ﷺ granted concession to the menstruating woman."
"1034","Tawoos narrated that I was with Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) when Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""Do you give the verdict that menstruating women should return before performing the last circumambulation (Tawaf) of the House (Ka'bah)?"" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""Yes."" Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Do not give such a verdict."" Upon this, Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""If not, then ask such-and-such Ansari woman whether the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave her this command?"" Tawoos said that Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) turned back laughing and said: ""I think you have spoken correctly."""
"1035","It is narrated from Tawus: He said, I was sitting with Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) when I heard him say that none of you should return until his last time is spent at the House of Allah (the Ka'bah). So I said, what is with him? Has he not heard what his companions have heard? Then the next year I (Tawus) sat with him again, and I heard him saying: They think that the Prophet ﷺ gave permission to the menstruating woman."
"1036","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: People were commanded that their last act (before leaving) should be at the House of Allah (in the form of the Farewell Tawaf), except that the Prophet ﷺ granted concession to menstruating women."
"1037","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) became menstruating after performing the Tawaf al-Ifadah, so I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Upon this, he (peace be upon him) said: ""Is she the one who will detain us?"" Then I said: O Messenger of Allah! She became menstruating after performing the Tawaf al-Ziyarah. He (peace be upon him) said: ""Then there is no (harm)."" Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us from Abdur Rahman bin Qasim in the same manner."
"1038","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) began menstruating on the Day of Sacrifice (10th of Dhul-Hijjah). So Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned her menstruation to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is she going to hold us back?"" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""She had already performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah and then menstruated."" So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then depart."""
"1039","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned Safiyyah bint Huyayy (may Allah be pleased with her), it was said to him that she has started menstruating. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps she will prevent us (from leaving)."" It was said to him that she has performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then there is no problem."""
"1040","Urwah narrated that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: While we were discussing why people bring women if there is no benefit for them, she said, ""If the matter were as you are saying, then there would be more than six thousand menstruating women in Mina."""
